<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy of Mauretania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 40 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy of Mauretania was the last king of Mauretania, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-ii">Juba II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-selene-ii">Cleopatra Selene</a> and a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Cleopatra. He ruled from about 23 CE as a Roman client king until the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> summoned him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and had him executed in 40 CE. A revolt led by his freedman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedemon">Aedemon</a> followed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> divided his kingdom into two provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-of-mauretania.jpg" alt="Ptolemy of Mauretania" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marie-Lan Nguyen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_of_Mauretania_Louvre_Ma1887.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
